* ideal_buck.sub -- an ideal synchronous buck power stage at a fixed duty.
*
* This is not a model of the TPS62130, and its provenance in the program says
* so: it is an assumption standing in for one. Two switches alternate at
* 1.25 MHz, the high side closed for 0.275 of each period, which is 3.3 V from
* 12 V. There is no control loop, so the duty never moves with the load or the
* input; no soft start, no current limit, no dead time, and no loss beyond the
* switches' on-resistance. BOOT, FB and EN are high-impedance: the bootstrap
* and the feedback divider are drawn on the board and draw nothing here.
*
* Ports, in the order an instance lists them: vin gnd sw boot fb en
.subckt ideal_buck vin gnd sw boot fb en
Vhigh hctl gnd PULSE(0 1 0 2n 2n 218n 800n)
Vlow lctl gnd PULSE(1 0 0 2n 2n 218n 800n)
Shigh vin sw hctl gnd switch
Slow sw gnd lctl gnd switch
.model switch SW(Ron=0.01 Roff=1e6 Vt=0.5 Vh=0.1)
Rboot boot sw 1e6
Rfb fb gnd 1e9
Ren en gnd 1e6
.ends ideal_buck
